Caramelized Zucchini and Sausage Pasta
  --Jamie Vespa

4 tbsp. evoo, divided
1/2 c panko breadcrumbs
1 lemon (zest and juice), divided
1 lb. zucchini, thinly sliced crosswise
12 oz. dry pasta of choice (short shape like shells or shellbows, orecchiette, or farfalle)
1 large shallot, diced (about 1/2 to 3/4 cup)
4 garlic cloves, minced
12 oz. raw chicken or turkey sausage (from 3 links), casings removed
1/2 c heavy cream
1/3 c grated Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese
1/2 c torn fresh basil leaves + more for garnish
kosher salt and cracked black pepper to taste

Bring a large pot of generously salted water to a boil. heat 1 tbsp evoo in a large skillet over medium. Add panko and cook, stirring often, until golden brown and toasted, ~3-5 min. Transfer to a bowl and stir in lemon zest and a pinch of salt. Set aside. Using the same pan, heat 2 tbsp evoo over medium heat. Add zucchini and cook, stirring only occasionally, until golden brown, ~10-12 min. (For optimal caramelization, resist the urge to stir too often. Let the zucchini cook undisturbed for ~3-4 min per side. This allows the natural sugars to release, and that rich, golden crust to form.) Season zucchini with salt and black pepper and transfer it to a bowl. This is a good time to begin cooking your pasta. Once al dente, reserve 1 c of pasta cooking water prior to draining. Add remaining 1 tbsp evoo to pan, along with shallots and garlic. Cook until aromatic, ~2-3 min. Add sausage and cook, breaking it up with a wooden spoon, until browned, ~5 min. Add heavy cream and a good pinch of salt and black pepper. Cook 2 min, scrapping to release any browned bits from the bottom of the pan. Add the pasta and 1/2 c of the reserved pasta water, toss well, and cook over medium-low heat until the sauce comes together, ~2 min. Stir in Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese, fresh basil, lemon juice, and ~2/3 of the zucchini (reserve extra for topping the pasta with). Add additional pasta water, a few tbsp at a time, if needed for a saucier consistency. Taste and season with additional salt and black pepper, if needed. (this pasta really benefits from a good dose of black pepper!) Spoon pasta into bowls and garnish with reserved caramelized zucchini, a sprinkle of lemony panko, extra fresh basil, and extra freshly grated Parmigiano-Reggiano cheese. Finish with a drizzle of extra-virgin olive oil and cracked black pepper, if desired.


Notes: probably want to double amount of zucchini and add red pepper flakes
